hadiths[287]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19714","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim dies except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, admits in his place into the Fire a Jew or a Christian."
"19715","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi Burdah and Awn ibn Utbah, that they both witnessed Abu Burdah narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz this hadith. Awn said: So he made him swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, that his father narrated it to him, that he heard it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Said did not object to Awn that he made him swear."
"19716","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, good and evil are two dispositions that will be set up for people on the Day of Resurrection. As for good, it will give glad tidings to its people and promise them good. And as for evil, it will say: To me, to me, and they will be able to do nothing for it except cling to it."
"19717","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Yazid, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, akhbarana Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer, then said: Stay in your places, remain firm. Then he went to the men and said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, commands me to command you to fear Allah the Exalted and to speak a right word. Then he went among the women and said to them: Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, commands me to command you to fear Allah and to speak a right word. He said: Then he returned until he came to the men and said: When you enter the mosques of the Muslims and their markets while you have arrows with you, then hold them by their blades, lest you strike anyone with them and harm him or wound him."
"19718","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathani my father, haddathana Husayn, from Ibn Buraydah, he said: I was told from al-Ashari that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Allah, I seek Your forgiveness for what I have put forward and what I have put back, and what I have concealed and what I have declared. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer, and You have power over all things."
"19719","Haddathana Hushaym, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, he said: Umar wrote in his will that no governor of mine shall remain more than a year, and keep al-Ashari, meaning Abu Musa, for four years."
"19720","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When there passes by you a funeral of a Jew or a Christian or a Muslim, then stand for it, for you do not stand for it itself; you only stand for those with it of the angels."
"19721","Haddathana Abd al-Samad and Affan, they said: Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, akhbarana Ali ibn Zayd, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, from al-Ashari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Hour there will be harj. They said: And what is harj. He said: Killing. They said: More than we kill; we kill every year more than seventy thousand. He said: It is not your killing of the polytheists, but killing of one another. They said: And will we have our minds with us on that day. He said: The minds of the people of that time will be taken away, and there will remain a rabble of people, most of whom will think they are upon something while they are upon nothing. Affan said in his hadith: Abu Musa said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, I find no way out for me and you from it, if it reaches me and you, except to come out of it as we entered into it, having shed no blood in it nor taken wealth."
"19722","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Mansur, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is the highest, then he is in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He."
"19723","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam, haddathana Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, he said: Abu Musa said: Ali ibn Abi Talib reminded us of a prayer we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; either we forgot it or we deliberately left it: he would say takbir every time he bowed and every time he rose and every time he prostrated."
"19724","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Yazid, haddathana Said ibn Abi Ayyub, he said: I heard a man from Quraysh called Abu Abd Allah, who used to sit with Jafar ibn Rabiah, he said: I heard Abu Burdah al-Ashari narrating from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The greatest of sins with Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, for a servant to meet Him with after the major sins He forbade, is that a man dies while owing a debt for which he leaves no payment."
"19725","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, haddathana al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: A man loves a people but has not yet joined them. So he said: A person is with whom he loves."
"19726","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, haddathana al-Amash, from Shaqiq, he said: Abd Allah and Abu Musa were sitting together, reviewing hadith, and Abu Musa said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Hour there will be days in which knowledge will be lifted and ignorance will descend, and harj will increase, and harj is killing."
"19727","Haddathana Yahya, meaning Ibn Adam, haddathana Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abu Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from al-Ashari, he said: Ibn Abi Talib reminded us, while we were in Basra, of a prayer we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: he would say takbir when he prostrated and when he stood. So I do not know whether we forgot it or deliberately left it."
"19728","Haddathana Yunus, haddathana Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, from Yunus and Thabit and Humayd and Habib, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Hour, then he mentioned something like the hadith of Abd al-Samad from Hammad from Ali ibn Zayd, except that he said: Abu Musa said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, I find no way for me and you, if I reach them, except to come out of them as we entered them, having shed no blood in them nor taken wealth."
"19729","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Sufyan, from Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When you pass by arrows in the markets of the Muslims or in their mosques, then hold them by the blades, lest you wound anyone with them."
"19730","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from his father, from a man, from Abu Musa, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"19731","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from his father, from a man, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised silk in his right hand and gold in his left and said: Permitted for the females of my nation and forbidden for its males."
"19732","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, haddathana Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from a man, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Gold and silk have been permitted for the females of my nation and forbidden for its males."
"19733","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Mamar, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, that Abu Musa al-Ashari led his companions in prayer, then mentioned the hadith, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and clarified our practice for us and taught us our prayer, and said: When you pray, then straighten your rows, then let one of you lead you, then he mentioned the hadith."
"19734","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana al-Thawri, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to the land of my people. Then when the Hajj came, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Hajj, and I performed Hajj, and I came to him while he was staying at al-Abtah. He said to me: With what did you enter ihram, O Abd Allah ibn Qays. He said: I said: Labbayk, with a Hajj like the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: You did well. Then he said: Did you bring a sacrificial animal. So I said: I did not do so. So he said to me: Go and circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then come out of ihram. So I went and did what he commanded me, and I went to a woman from my people, and she washed my head with marshmallow and deloused it. Then I entered ihram for Hajj on the day of Tarwiyah. And I kept giving fatwa to people with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me, until he passed away, then the time of Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, then the time of Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him. While I was standing at the Black Stone or the Maqam, giving fatwa to people with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me, a man came to me and spoke to me privately and said: Do not hasten with your fatwa, for the Commander of the Believers has introduced something in the rites. So I said: O people, whomever we gave a fatwa to about the rites, let him wait, for the Commander of the Believers is coming, so follow him. He said: So Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, came, and I said: O Commander of the Believers, did you introduce something in the rites. He said: Yes, that we hold to the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, for it commands completion, and that we hold to the practice of our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for he did not come out of ihram until he sacrificed the sacrificial animal."
"19735","Haddathana Waki, from Harmalah ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abu Musa, he said: There were two securities in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; one was lifted and the other remains: And Allah would not punish them while you are among them, and Allah would not punish them while they seek forgiveness."
"19736","Haddathana Surayj, haddathana Abd Allah, meaning al-Umari, from Nafi, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from a man from Basra, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Silk and gold have been permitted for the females of my nation and forbidden for its males."
"19737","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Sufyan, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his brother, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: Two men from my people came with me. He said: So we came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they addressed and spoke, hinting at seeking office. So the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed, or it was seen in his face. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most treacherous of you to me is one who seeks it. So upon you is fear of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He. He said: And he did not seek their help for anything."
"19738","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Mamar, from Qatadah, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I think he said: in a garden, and a man came and greeted. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Go and give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I went, and behold it was Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him. So I said: Enter and receive glad tidings of Paradise. And he kept praising Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, until he sat down. Then another came and greeted, and he said: Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I went, and behold it was Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him. So I said: Enter and receive glad tidings of Paradise. And he kept praising Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, until he sat down. Then another came and greeted, and he said: Go and give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise for a severe trial. He said: So I went, and behold it was Uthman. So I said: Enter and receive glad tidings of Paradise for a severe trial. He said: So he kept saying: O Allah, patience, until he sat down."
"19739","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Mamar, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Abd Allah ibn Qays Abu Musa al-Ashari greeted Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them, three times, and he was not given permission, so he returned. So Umar sent after him: Why did you return. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When one of you greets three times and is not answered, let him return."
"19740","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Mamar, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the imam says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then say: Our Lord, to You is praise; Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, will hear for you. For Allah the Exalted decreed upon the tongue of His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Allah hears whoever praises Him."
"19741","Haddathana Hammad ibn Usamah, from Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burdah, from his grandfather Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The trustworthy treasurer who gives what he is commanded in full, complete, with his soul content with it, until he hands it to the one for whom he was commanded, is one of the givers of charity."
"19742","Haddathana Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari, akhbarana Thabit ibn Umarah al-Hanafi, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every eye commits adultery."
"19743","Haddathana Husayn ibn Ali, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: Two men disputed before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, over land, one of them from Hadramawt. He said: So he assigned the oath to one of them. He said: So the other cried out and said: Then he will take my land. So he said: If he seizes it with his oath unjustly, he will be among those whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, will not look at on the Day of Resurrection nor purify, and for him is a painful punishment. He said: And the other was cautious and gave it back."
"19744","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, haddathana Ubayd Allah, from Nafi, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Silk and gold are forbidden for the males of my nation and permitted for their females."
"19745","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The orphan girl is to be consulted about herself; if she remains silent, she has given permission, and if she refuses, she is not to be coerced."
"19746","Haddathana Waki and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Feed the hungry, release the captive, and visit the sick. Abd al-Rahman said: The sick."
"19747","Haddathana Waki and Abd al-Rahman, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"19748","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, from Abu Musa, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eating chicken."
"19749","Haddathana Waki, from Sufyan, from Asim, meaning al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and we overlooked a valley, and he mentioned something of its terror, and people began saying takbir and tahlil. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, be gentle with yourselves. And they raised their voices, so he said: O people, you do not call upon one deaf nor absent; He is with you."
"19750","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Usamah ibn Zayd, haddathana Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever plays with backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"19751","Haddathana Attab, haddathana Abd Allah, akhbarana Usamah ibn Zayd, haddathani Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Murrah, freedman of Aqil, as far as I know, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever plays with backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"19752","Haddathana Waki and Ibn Jafar, they said: Thana Shubah, from Amr, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Many men have attained perfection, but no women have attained perfection except Asiyah the wife of Firawn and Maryam the daughter of Imran. And the excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over other food."
"19753","Haddathana Waki, from al-Masudi, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that when Asma came, Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, met her on one of the roads of Madinah and said: The Abyssinian woman, is it. She said: Yes. So he said: What fine people you are, were it not that you preceded in migration. So she said to Umar: You were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he carried your foot-soldier and taught your ignorant, while we fled with our religion. Indeed I shall not return until I mention that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So she returned to him and told him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rather, you have two migrations: your migration to Madinah and your migration to Abyssinia."
"19754","Haddathana Waki, from al-Masudi, and Yazid said: Anbaana al-Masudi, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named himself names for us, among them what we memorized, and said: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Muqaffi, and al-Hashir, and the Prophet of Mercy. Yazid said: And the Prophet of Repentance, and the Prophet of Battle."
"19755","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but has not yet joined them. He said: A person is with whom he loves."
"19756","Haddathana Waki, haddathana al-Amash, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No one is more patient with harm he hears than Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He; partners are ascribed to Him while He provides for them."
"19757","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Sufyan, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from a man, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The passing of my nation is by piercing and plague. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, this piercing we know, so what is plague. He said: The stabbing of your enemies from the jinn, and in each are martyrs."
"19758","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Shubah, and Ibn Jafar, akhbarana Shubah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, Ibn Jafar said in his hadith: I heard Abu Ubaydah narrating from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah the Exalted extends His Hand at night for the wrongdoer of the day to repent, and extends His Hand in the day for the wrongdoer of the night to repent, until the sun rises from its setting place."
"19759","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Jafar, they said: Thana Shubah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us with four, and said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, does not sleep, nor is it fitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the balance and raises it. To Him is raised the deed of the night by day and the deed of the day by night."
"19760","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Shubah, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon every Muslim is charity. He said: What if he does not find. He said: He works with his hand, so he benefits himself and gives charity. He said: What if he cannot do. He said: He helps the needy distressed one. He said: What if he does not do. He said: He commands good, or justice. He said: What if he cannot do. He said: He withholds from evil, for that is charity for him."
"19761","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Salih al-Thawri, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever has a slave girl and teaches her and teaches her well, and disciplines her and disciplines her well, then frees her and marries her, then for him are two rewards. And a slave who fulfills the right of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, and the right of his masters. And a man from the People of the Book who believed in what Isa brought and what Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, brought, then for him are two rewards."
"19762","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A person is with whom he loves."
"19763","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was halting at al-Abtah. So he said to me: Did you perform Hajj. I said: Yes. He said: So with what did you enter ihram. He said: I said: Labbayk, with an ihram like the ihram of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: You did well. He said: Circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, then come out of ihram. He said: So I circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, then I went to a woman from Banu Qays, and she deloused my head. Then I entered ihram for Hajj. He said: And I used to give fatwa to people with it until the caliphate of Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him. Then a man said: O Abu Musa, or O Abd Allah ibn Qays, go slowly with some of your fatwa, for you do not know what the Commander of the Believers has introduced concerning the rites after you. He said: So he said: O people, whomever we gave a fatwa to, let him wait, for the Commander of the Believers is coming to you, so follow him. He said: So Umar came, and I mentioned that to him. So he said: If we hold to the Book of Allah, then the Book of Allah the Exalted commands us with completion. And if we hold to the practice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not come out of ihram until the sacrificial animal reached its place."
"19764","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Yazid ibn Aws, from Abu Musa, that he fell unconscious, and the mother of his child wept over him. Then when he recovered, he said to her: Has it not reached you what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. He said: So I asked her, and she said: He is not from us who raises his voice in lamentation, and shaves, and tears."
"19765","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever hears of me from my nation, or a Jew or a Christian, and does not believe in me, will not enter Paradise."
"19766","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, from Abu al-Tayyah, haddathani a tall black man, Abu al-Tayyah describing him, that he came with Ibn Abbas to Basra, and he wrote to Abu Musa, and Abu Musa wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was walking and turned to soft ground beside a wall and urinated. Then he said: The Children of Israil, when one of them urinated and something of his urine touched him, he would follow it and cut it with scissors. And he said: When one of you wants to urinate, let him seek out a place for his urine."
"19767","Haddathana Bahz, haddathana Jafar ibn Sulayman, haddathana Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays, he said: I heard my father, while facing the enemy, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The gates of Paradise are under the shade of swords. He said: So a man from the people, shabby in appearance, stood and said: O Abu Musa, did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes. He said: So he returned to his companions and said: I bid you farewell with peace. Then he broke the scabbard of his sword and threw it away, then walked with his sword and struck with it until he was killed."
"19768","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shubah, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Yazid ibn Aws, he said: Abu Musa fell unconscious, and they wept over him. So he said: I am free from those whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, declared himself free from. So they asked his wife about that, and she said: Whoever shaves, or tears, or raises his voice in lamentation."
"19769","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shubah, from Awf, from Khalid al-Ahdhab, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, he said: Abu Musa fell unconscious, and they wept over him. Then he recovered and said: I declare myself innocent to you from those whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, declared himself innocent from: whoever shaves, or tears, or raises his voice in lamentation."
"19770","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Awf, and Hammad ibn Usamah, haddathani Awf, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Abu Kinanah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at the door of a house in which there were a group from Quraysh, and he took hold of the two doorposts, then said: Is there in the house anyone but a Qurashi. He said: So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, except so-and-so, the son of our sister. So he said: The son of the sister of a people is from them. He said: Then he said: This matter is in Quraysh as long as they, when shown mercy they are merciful, and when they judge they are just, and when they divide they are fair. So whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; neither repentance nor ransom will be accepted from him."
"19771","Haddathana Abu Muawiyah, haddathana al-Amash, from Shaqiq, he said: I was sitting with Abu Musa and Abd Allah, and Abu Musa said: Did you not hear the saying of Ammar: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand, and I became junub and did not find water, so I rolled in the dust as an animal rolls. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. So he said: It would have sufficed you to say, and he struck with his hand on the earth, then wiped each one of them with its companion, then wiped his face with them. Al-Amash did not go beyond the two hands."
"19772","Haddathana Abu Muawiyah, haddathana al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a man who fights out of bravery, and fights out of zeal, and fights out of show. Which of that is in the path of Allah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, is the highest, then he is in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He."
"19773","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Talhah ibn Yahya, he said: Akhbarani Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Muadh and Abu Musa to Yemen, and commanded them to teach people the Quran."
"19774","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, haddathana Burayd ibn Abd Allah, haddathana Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: When one of you passes with arrows in our mosques or our markets, let him hold with his hand over their heads, lest he injure anyone."
"19775","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, haddathana Burayd ibn Abd Allah, haddathana Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: Keep to this Quran, for by the One in whose Hand is my soul, it escapes more swiftly than one of you does from camels from their hobbles. Abu Ahmad said: I said to Burayd: These hadiths you narrated to me from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: They are from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but I will not say that to you."
"19776","Haddathana Mutamir ibn Sulayman al-Taymi, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah the hadith of Abu Hariz, that Abu Burdah narrated to him, he said: Abu Musa enjoined when death came to him, and said: When you set out with my funeral, hasten the walking, and no incense burner shall follow me, and do not place in my grave anything that stands between me and the dust, and do not place a building over my grave. And I call you to witness that I am free from every woman who shaves, or raises her voice in lamentation, or tears. They said: Did you hear anything about it. He said: Yes, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"19777","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Sufyan, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at al-Batha. So he said: With what did you enter ihram. So I said: With an ihram like the ihram of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said: Did you bring a sacrificial animal. I said: No. He said: Circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, then come out of ihram."
"19778","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Said, from Qatadah, he said: Thana Anas ibn Malik, that Abu Musa al-Ashari said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the believer who recites the Quran is like the citron: its taste is good and its scent is good. And the example of the believer who does not recite the Quran is like the date: its taste is good and it has no scent. And the example of the wicked one who recites the Quran is like basil: its taste is bitter and its scent is good. And the example of the wicked one who does not recite the Quran is like the colocynth: its taste is bitter and it has no scent."
"19779","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, haddathana Shubah, from Ghalib al-Tammar, he said: I heard Masruq ibn Aws, or Aws ibn Masruq, a man from Banu Yarbu, narrating that he heard Abu Musa al-Ashari narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The fingers are equal. So I said to Ghalib: Ten, ten. So he said: Yes."
"19780","Haddathana Abu Nuh, akhbarana Malik, from Musa ibn Maysarah, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever plays with backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"19781","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, haddathana al-Mubarak, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Perform ablution from what fire has changed the color of."
"19782","Haddathana Yunus ibn Muhammad and Affan, they said: Thana Hammad ibn Salamah, from Asim, Affan said: Akhbarana Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to be guarded by his companions, and he mentioned the hadith."
"19783","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, haddathana Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, that a man came while he was eating chicken, and withdrew. So he said: I swore not to eat it; I saw it eating something filthy. So he said: Come near, for I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eating it."
"19784","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, he said: It was said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: A man loves a people but has not yet joined them. He said: A person is with whom he loves."
"19785","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Talhah ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Let one of you seek permission three times; if he is given permission, otherwise let him return."
"19786","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, haddathana Shubah, from Ghalib, from Aws ibn Masruq, or Masruq ibn Aws al-Yarbui, from Banu Tamim, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The fingers are equal. Shubah said: I said to him: Ten, ten. He said: Yes."
"19787","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Harb, haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd, haddathani Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among a group of Asharis, seeking mounts from him. So he said: No, by Allah, I shall not mount you, and I have nothing with me to mount you upon. So we remained as long as Allah willed. Then he ordered for us three young she-camels with white humps. Then when we departed, some of us said to others: We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking mounts, and he swore not to mount us. Go back with us, that we may remind him. He said: So we came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we came to you seeking mounts, and you swore not to mount us, then you mounted us. So he said: I did not mount you; rather Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, mounted you. By Allah, if Allah wills the Exalted, I do not swear an oath and then see another better than it, except I do what is better and expiate my oath, or he said: except I expiate my oath and do what is better."
"19788","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, haddathana Musa ibn Ayan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from a man, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever guards what is between his jaws and his private part will enter Paradise."
"19789","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah, that Awn and Said ibn Abi Burdah narrated to him that they both witnessed Abu Burdah narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No Muslim man dies except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, admits in his place into the Fire a Jew or a Christian. He said: So Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz made him swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, three times, that his father narrated it to him from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he swore to him. He said: And Said did not narrate to me that he made him swear, and he did not object to Awn's statement."
"19790","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, from Ghalib al-Tammar, he said: I heard Aws ibn Masruq, a man from us who had taken two dirhams in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and raided in his caliphate, narrating from Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The fingers are equal. Shubah said: So I said: Ten, ten. He said: Yes."
"19791","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shubah, akhbarani Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever hears of me from my nation, or a Jew or a Christian, then does not believe in me, will enter the Fire."
"19792","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Hammam, haddathana a man from the Ansar, that Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays narrated to him that his father narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit the Ansar often, privately and publicly. When he visited privately, he would come to a man in his house, and when he visited publicly, he would come to the mosque."
"19793","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, haddathana Abu Zubayd, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has a slave girl and frees her and marries her, for him are two rewards."
"19794","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said, haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Abu Musa, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever does a good deed and is pleased by it, and does an evil deed and is grieved by it, then he is a believer."
"19795","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, haddathana Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi, from Mujammi ibn Yahya ibn Zayd ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, he said: I heard him mentioning it from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then we said: If only we waited until we pray Isha with him. He said: So we waited, and he came out to us and said: You have remained here. We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; we said: we shall pray Isha with you. He said: You did well, or you were right. Then he raised his head to the sky, and he said: And he often used to raise his head to the sky, and said: The stars are a security for the sky; when the stars go, there comes to the sky what it is promised. And I am a security for my companions; when I go, there comes to my companions what they are promised. And my companions are a security for my nation; when my companions go, there comes to my nation what it is promised."
"19796","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, haddathana al-Walid ibn Muslim, haddathana Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Urdunni, from Abd Allah ibn Nuaym al-Qaysi, he said: Haddathani al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Arzab al-Ashari, that Abu Musa narrated to them, he said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, defeated Hawazin at Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed Abu Amir al-Ashari over the cavalry of pursuit, and he pursued. And I was among those who pursued them. His horse was swift with him, and he caught up with Ibn Durayd ibn al-Simmah, but he killed Abu Amir and took the banner. And I attacked Ibn Durayd and killed him and took the banner, and returned with the people. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me carrying the banner, he said: O Abu Musa, Abu Amir was killed. He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raise his hands, supplicating, saying: O Allah, Your servant Ubayd, Abu Amir, make him among the most numerous on the Day of Resurrection."
"19797","Haddathana Bahz, haddathana Shubah, haddathana Abu al-Tayyah, from an elder of theirs, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to soft ground beside a wall and urinated. Shubah said: So I said to Abu al-Tayyah: Sitting. He said: I do not know. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Children of Israil, when urine touched them, would cut it with scissors. So when one of you urinates, let him seek out a place for his urine."
"19798","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, haddathana al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from the hadith of Abu Hariz, that Abu Burdah narrated to him, from the hadith of Abu Musa, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three do not enter Paradise: the habitual drinker of wine, and the severer of kinship, and the believer in magic. And whoever dies habitual in wine, Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, will give him to drink from the river of al-Ghutah. It was said: And what is the river of al-Ghutah. He said: A river flowing from the private parts of prostitutes, the smell of their private parts harming the people of the Fire."
"19799","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, haddathana Abu Usamah, from Burayd ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: A boy was born to me, so I brought him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he named him Ibrahim and rubbed his palate with a date."
"19800","And he said: A house burned in Madinah with its people, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was told of their affair, so he said: This fire is an enemy to you; when you sleep, extinguish it from yourselves."
"19801","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he would send one of his Companions on some matter of his, would say: Give glad tidings and do not drive away, and make easy and do not make difficult."
"19802","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of what Allah Almighty has sent me with of guidance and knowledge is like rain that fell upon land, and part of it accepted it and produced herbage and abundant grass, and part of it was barren tracts that held the water, so Allah Almighty benefited people thereby, and they drank and pastured and watered and sowed and irrigated, and another part of it was only smooth plains that hold no water and grow no herbage. So that is the likeness of one who gained understanding in the religion of Allah Almighty and was benefited by Allah Almighty through what I was sent with and benefited thereby, so he learned and taught, and the likeness of one who did not lift his head with that and did not accept the guidance of Allah Almighty with which I was sent."
"19803","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abbad, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Musa, who said: I brought ablution water to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he performed ablution and prayed and said: O Allah, set right my religion for me, and make ample for me in my means, and bless for me in my provision."
"19804","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Ali ibn Zayd and al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise. He said: And what is it. He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"19805","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Qays al-Ashari, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tent is a hollow pearl, its height into the sky sixty miles, in every corner of it the believer has a family whom the others do not see. And perhaps Affan said: For every corner."
"19806","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes through a mosque or a market or a gathering with arrows in his hand, let him hold them by their blades. Abu Musa said: By Allah, we did not die until some of us aimed them at the faces of others."
"19807","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Thabit, meaning Ibn Umarah, from Ghunaym, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a woman perfumes herself and goes out before people so they find her scent, she is such and such."
"19808","Yahya narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Ghiyath: Abu Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Shall I guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise, or do you know what a treasure from the treasures of Paradise is. I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"19809","Yahya informed us: Ubaydullah informed us: Nafi informed me, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us: Nafi narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"19810","Yahya, he is Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, that Abu Musa sought permission from Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, three times, and he was not given permission, so he went back. He said: Did I not hear the voice of Abdullah ibn Qays just now. They said: Yes. He said: Then seek him. He said: So they sought him and he was called. He said: What carried you to do what you did. He said: I sought permission three times and was not given permission, so I went back; we were commanded with this. He said: You shall surely bring proof of it or I shall surely do such. He said: So he came to a mosque or a gathering of the Ansar, and they said: None but the youngest of us will testify for you. So Abu Said al-Khudri stood and testified for him. Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said: This was hidden from me of the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); trading in the markets distracted me from it."
"19811","Yahya ibn Said and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Awf narrated to us, he said: Qasamah ibn Zuhayr narrated to me, Ibn Jafar said: From Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty created Adam from a handful which He took from all the earth, so the children of Adam came according to the earth; among them came the white and the red and the black and what is between that, and the wicked and the good, and the soft and the hard, and what is between that."
"19812","Rawh narrated to us: Awf narrated to us, from Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, he said: I heard al-Ashari, and he mentioned the like of it."
"19813","Waki narrated to us: Burayd ibn Abi Burdah ibn Abi Musa narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a questioner asked him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intercede and you will be rewarded, and let Allah Almighty decree upon the tongue of His Prophet what He loves."
"19814","Waki narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, who said: Abu Musa al-Ashari said: Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, reminded us of a prayer we prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); either we forgot it or we abandoned it deliberately; he would say the takbir whenever he bowed and when he prostrated and when he rose."
"19815","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Hakim ibn Daylam, from Abu Burdah, from his father, who said: The Jews would pretend to sneeze before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), hoping he would say to them: May Allah have mercy on you, but he would say to them: May Allah guide you and set right your state."
"19816","Waki narrated to us: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not sleep, nor is it befitting for Him to sleep; He lowers the balance and raises it. His veil is fire; if He uncovered it, the splendors of His Face would burn everything His sight reached. Then Abu Ubaydah recited: Blessed is whoever is in the fire and whoever is around it, and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"19817","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, who said: Abu Musa said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while I thought that Abdullah was of the household, or what he mentioned of this."
"19818","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no one more patient with harm he hears than Allah Almighty; they claim a son for Him, yet He grants them health and provides for them."
"19819","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that a brother of Abu Musa would rush into strife, and he kept forbidding him but he would not stop. He said: If I thought a little from me would suffice you, or he said: of admonition, apart from what I see. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims meet with their swords, and one of them kills the other, the killer and the killed are in the Fire. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer, so what of the killed. He said: He intended to kill his companion."
"19820","Ismail narrated to us: Ayyub informed us, from al-Qasim al-Tamimi, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: We were with Abu Musa, and he presented in his food chicken meat, and among the people was a man of Banu Taym Allah, red as if he were a freedman, and he did not come near. Abu Musa said to him: Come near, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating from it. He said: I saw it eating something and I found it foul, so I swore never to eat it. He said: Come near; I shall inform you about that. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group of the Asharis seeking mounts from him, while he was distributing camels of the charity. Ayyub said: I think him angry. He said: No, by Allah, I shall not carry you, and I have nothing with which to carry you. So we left, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought spoils of camels. He said: Where are these Asharis. So we came, and he ordered for us five white-humped camels, and we set out. I said to my companions: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking mounts, and he swore not to carry us, then he sent to us and carried us. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forgot his oath; by Allah, if we take the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unawares in his oath, we shall never prosper. Return with us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and remind him of his oath. So we returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we came to you seeking mounts, and you swore not to carry us, then you carried us, so we knew, or we thought, that you forgot your oath. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go forth, for Allah Almighty is the one who carried you. And I, by Allah, if Allah wills, do not swear an oath and then see another better than it except that I do what is better and expiate it."
"19821","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: I was with Abu Musa, and food containing chicken was brought near to him, and he mentioned its meaning."
"19822","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us: Abu Qilabah narrated to me, from a man of Banu Taym Allah called Zahdam, who said: We were with Abu Musa, and chicken meat was brought, and he mentioned it."
"19823","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah and from al-Qasim al-Tamimi, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: Between us and al-Ashari there was brotherhood, and he mentioned the hadith and its meaning."
"19824","Ismail narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us our prayer and our practice. He said: The imam is only to be followed, so when he says the takbir, say the takbir, and when he says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, say: Amin, Allah Almighty will answer you. And when he bows, bow, and when he rises, rise, and when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise, Allah will hear for you. And when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he rises, rise, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is for that."
"19825","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Affan narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, Affan said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abu Wail, he said: Abu Musa al-Ashari narrated to us that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights for spoils, and a man fights to be mentioned, and a man fights so his place may be seen; so who is in the path of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is the highest, he is in the path of Allah Almighty."
"19826","Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group of my people, and he said: Receive glad tidings and give glad tidings to those behind you: whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, truthful in it, will enter Paradise. So we went out from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving glad tidings to the people, then Umar ibn al-Khattab met us, so he brought us back to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, then the people will rely. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent."
"19827","Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us: al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, there are drinks there; what shall I drink and what shall I leave. He said: And what are they. I said: Al-bit and al-mizr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not know what they were, so he said: What is al-bit and what is al-mizr. He said: As for al-bit, it is millet wine cooked until it becomes bit; and as for al-mizr, it is honey wine. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not drink any intoxicant."
"19828","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi Abu Muhammad narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and we would not ascend a height nor rise upon a height nor descend into a valley except that we raised our voices with the takbir. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near to us and said: O people, be gentle with yourselves, for you do not call upon one deaf nor absent; you call upon One hearing, seeing. The one you call is nearer to each of you than the neck of his mount. O Abdullah ibn Qays, shall I not teach you a word from the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"19829","Abu al-Mughirah, he is al-Nadr ibn Ismail, meaning al-Qass, narrated to us: Burayd narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, no believer will remain but a Jew or a Christian will be brought until he is handed to him, and it will be said to him: This is your ransom from the Fire. Abu Burdah said: So Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz made me swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, did you hear Abu Musa mentioning it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: Yes, so Umar was pleased with that."
"19830","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ashari, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to give extra spoils in his campaigns. Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Salih, that he used to give extra spoils in his campaigns."
"19831","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Salih, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three will be given their rewards twice: a man who had a slave girl and disciplined her and disciplined her well, and taught her and taught her well, then freed her and married her; and a slave who gives the right of his Lord Almighty and the right of his masters; and a man who believed in his scripture and in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Al-Shabi said to me: Take it for nothing; even if you traveled for it to Kirman, that would be little."
"19832","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from his father, that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over an animal, neither of them having proof, so he made it between them in halves."
"19833","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Uthman ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know, or shall I guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise. He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"19834","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, that they were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and they raised their voices in supplication. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You do not call upon one deaf nor absent; you call upon One near, responsive, who hears your supplication and answers. Then he said: O Abdullah ibn Qays, or O Abu Musa, shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"19835","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman al-Azrami, narrated to us, from Abu Ali, a man of Banu Kahil, who said: Abu Musa al-Ashari addressed us and said: O people, fear this association, for it is more hidden than the crawling of ants. Abdullah ibn Hazn and Qays ibn al-Mudarib stood up to him and said: By Allah, you shall surely retract what you said, or we shall surely go to Umar, whether we are permitted or not permitted. He said: Rather I retract what I said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us one day and said: O people, fear this association, for it is more hidden than the crawling of ants. One whom Allah willed to speak said to him: And how shall we fear it when it is more hidden than the crawling of ants, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: O Allah, we seek refuge in You from associating with You anything we know, and we seek Your forgiveness for what we do not know."
"19836","Waki narrated to us, from Harmalah ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abu Musa, who said: There were two securities in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them was lifted and the other remains: And Allah would not punish them while you are among them, and Allah would not punish them while they seek forgiveness."
"19837","Affan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from one who heard Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, who said: Abu Musa said: I said to a companion of mine: Come, let us make this day of ours for Allah Almighty. It was as if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) witnessed us, and he said: And among them is one who says: Come, let us make this day of ours for Allah Almighty. He kept repeating it until I wished I could sink into the earth."
"19838","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah: al-Hasan narrated to us that Abu Musa al-Ashari had a brother called Abu Ruhm, and he would rush into strife, and al-Ashari disliked strife. He said to him: Were it not for what you conveyed to me, I would not have told you: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No two Muslims who meet with their swords, and one of them kills the other, except that they both enter the Fire together."
"19839","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Masruq ibn Aws, that Abu Musa reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning fingers: ten, ten, of camels."
"19840","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: Abu Musa sought permission from Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both. He said: Once, twice, thrice, then Abu Musa went back. Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said to him: You shall surely bring proof of this or I shall surely do such, as if saying: I shall make you an example in the horizons. So Abu Musa went to a gathering in which were the Ansar, and mentioned that to them. He said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you seeks permission three times and is not given permission, let him go back. They said: Yes; none but the youngest of us shall stand with you. He said: So Abu Said al-Khudri stood to Umar and said: This is Abu Said, so he let him go."
"19841","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Layth, he said: I heard Abu Burdah reporting from his father, who said: People passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a funeral, hurrying with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tranquility should be upon you."
"19842","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from his grandfather, who said: I heard Abu Musa saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not accept the prayer of a man with any khaluq perfume on his body."
"19843","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that Abu Musa al-Ashari reported to him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of the believer who recites the Quran is like the citron, its taste good and its scent good. And the likeness of the believer who does not recite the Quran is like the date, its taste good and it has no scent. And the likeness of the wicked one who recites the Quran is like basil, its scent good and its taste bitter. And the likeness of the wicked one who does not recite the Quran is like the colocynth, its taste bitter and it has no scent."
"19844","Affan narrated to us: Aban narrated to us with both of these, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19845","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Yazid ibn Aws, who said: Abu Musa fainted and they wept over him. He said: I am free of whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was free. They asked his wife about that, what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. She said: Do you not know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. She said: From her who shaves and wails and tears."
"19846","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Awf, he said: I heard Khalid al-Ahdab, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, who said: Abu Musa fainted and they wept over him, then he regained consciousness and said: I absolve myself to you of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) absolved himself: from her who shaves and wails and tears. And Affan narrated them both to us another time, and he said in both of them: From her who shaves or wails or tears."
"19847","Affan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us: Asim informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be guarded by his Companions. I stood one night and did not see him in his sleeping place, and I was seized by what is old and what is new, so I went to look, and I found Muadh who had met what I met. We heard a sound like the grinding of a mill, and they both stood in their place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from the direction of the sound and said: Do you know where I was and in what I was. One coming from my Lord Almighty came to me and gave me choice between half my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. They said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah Almighty to make us in your intercession. He said: You, and whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, are in my intercession."
"19848","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty extends His Hand by day so the offender of the night may repent, and extends His Hand by night so the offender of the day may repent, until the sun rises from its west."
"19849","Ismail narrated to us: Ghalib al-Tammar narrated to us, from Masruq ibn Aws, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Concerning fingers: ten, ten."
"19850","Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: al-Masudi narrated to us, and my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Masudi informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named himself names for us, some of which we remembered and some of which we did not remember. He said: I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and al-Muqaffi, and al-Hashir, and the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of battle."
"19851","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Abu al-Salil, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, who said: We went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking mounts from him. He said: By Allah, I shall not carry you. So we returned, then he sent to us three white-humped camels. Some of us said to others: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore not to carry us. So we came to him and said: You swore not to carry us. He said: I did not carry you; Allah Almighty is the one who carried you. There is no oath on earth that I swear, then see another better than it, except that I do it."
"19852","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us: Shubah al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: We were with Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, and he said: O my sons, shall I not report to you a hadith my father reported to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Whoever frees a slave, Allah Almighty frees, for every limb of it, a limb of him from the Fire."
"19853","Sufyan narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, as a report: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"19854","And the likeness of the good companion is like the perfume seller: if he does not give you of his perfume, its scent clings to you. And the likeness of the bad companion is like the bellows: if it does not burn you, some of its sparks reach you."
"19855","And the trustworthy treasurer who delivers what he is commanded, seeking reward thereby, is one of the givers of charity."
"19856","Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Burayd, from his grandfather, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"19857","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from al-Qarthaa, who said: When Abu Musa al-Ashari grew heavy, his wife cried out. He said to her: Do you not know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. She said: Yes, then she fell silent. When he died, she was asked: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say. She said: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed her who shaves or tears or wails."
"19858","Ismail informed us: Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us our prayer and our practice. He said: The imam is only to be followed, so when he says the takbir, say the takbir, and when he says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, say: Amin, Allah Almighty will answer you. And when he bows, bow, and when he rises, rise, and when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, Allah will hear for you. And when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he rises, rise, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is for that."
"19859","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, have you seen a man who loves a people but has not yet joined them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves. My father said:"
"19860","And likewise Waki narrated it to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa."
"19861","And Muhammad ibn Ubayd also, from Abu Musa."
"19862","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A person is with whom he loves."
"19863","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ahead of you are days in which ignorance will descend and knowledge will be lifted and harj will be abundant. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is harj. He said: Killing."
"19864","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who fights out of bravery, and fights out of zeal, and fights for show; which of that is in the path of Allah Almighty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is the highest, he is in the path of Allah Almighty."
"19865","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us with five words. He said: Allah Almighty does not sleep, nor is it befitting for Him to sleep, but He lowers the balance and raises it. The deed of the night is raised to Him before the deed of the day, and the deed of the day before the deed of the night. His veil is light; if He uncovered it, the splendors of His Face would burn what His sight reached of His creation."
"19866","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one more patient with harm he hears than Allah Almighty; He is associated with and a son is made for Him, yet He grants them health and repels from them and provides for them."
"19867","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Mamar ibn Rashid informed us, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will be given their reward twice: a man who believed in the first Book and the last Book; and a man who had a slave girl and disciplined her and disciplined her well, then freed her and married her; and a slave owned who worshiped his Lord well and advised his master, or as he said."
"19868","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with people of my tribe, after he conquered Khaybar by three days, and he allotted shares to us, and he did not divide for anyone who did not witness the conquest besides us."
"19869","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Usayd ibn al-Mutashammis said: We came with Abu Musa from Isbahan, and we hurried, and Uqaylah came. Abu Musa said: Is there no youth to lodge his kinswoman, meaning he said: a slave girl of al-Ashari. He said: I said: Yes, so I brought her near a tree and lodged her, then I came and sat with the people. He said: Shall I not report to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to report to us. We said: Yes, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to report to us that before the Hour is harj. It was said: And what is harj. He said: Lying and killing. They said: More than we kill now. He said: It is not your killing of the disbelievers, but it is some of you killing others, until a man kills his neighbor and kills his brother and kills his uncle and kills his cousin. They said: Glory be to Allah, and will we have our minds with us. He said: No, except that He will remove the minds of the people of that time, until one of you thinks he is upon something while he is upon nothing. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I feared those matters would overtake me and you, and I find for me and for you no way out of them, in what our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to us, except that we leave them as we entered them, not innovating anything in them."
"19870","Ismail narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Qasim al-Tamimi, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: We were with Abu Musa, and he presented his food, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Zahdam."
"19871","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: Ayyub said: And al-Qasim al-Kalbi reported it to me, from Zahdam. He said: I remember the hadith of al-Qasim better. He said: We were with Abu Musa, and he presented his food, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Zahdam."
"19872","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: Ayyub said: And al-Qasim al-Kalbi reported it to me, from Zahdam. He said: I remember the hadith of al-Qasim better. He said: We were with Abu Musa, and he called for his table, and it was brought with chicken meat upon it, and he mentioned the hadith."
"19873","Ismail narrated to us: Layth informed us, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father, that he said: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), shaken as a waterskin is shaken. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Moderation upon you."
"19874","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan: Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free the captive, and feed the hungry, and visit the sick."
"19875","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Awf narrated to us: Qasamah ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19876","Hawdhah narrated it to us: Awf narrated to us, from Qasamah, he said: I heard al-Ashari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty created Adam from a handful which He took from all the earth, so the children of Adam came according to the earth; among them He made the red and the white and the black and what is between that, and the soft and the hard and what is between that, and the wicked and the good and what is between that."
"19877","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Ghiyath: Abu Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Musa, that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a garden, with a stick in the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) striking between water and mud. A man came seeking to open, and he said: Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and it was Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him. He said: So I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then a man came seeking to open, and he said: Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and it was Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then a man came and sought to open, and he said: Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise for a trial that will befall him, or a trial that will be. He said: And it was Uthman, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise and informed him, and he said: Allah is the one whose help is sought."
"19878","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Uthman, meaning Ibn Ghiyath, narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a garden of the gardens of Medina, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Yahya, except that he said in the saying of Uthman, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him: Allah is the one whose help is sought, O Allah patience, and upon Allah is reliance."
"19879","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Wearing silk and gold is made lawful for the women of my nation and forbidden for its males."
"19880","Yahya narrated to us: Thabit, meaning Ibn Umarah, narrated to us: Ghunaym ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every eye is adulterous."
"19881","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Qurrah narrated to us: Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from his father, who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The people of Yemen have two drinks, or drinks: this al-bit of honey, and al-mizr of corn and barley; what do you command me concerning them. He said: I forbid you every intoxicant."
"19882","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, who said: The people took to a pass or a mountain path, and whenever a man rose upon it he called: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon a mule, turning it among the horses. He said: O people, you do not call upon one deaf nor absent. Then he said: O Abu Musa, or O Abdullah ibn Qays, shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise. He said: I said: Yes. He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"19883","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Juayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Humayd ibn Bashir, from al-Muharrar, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None turns its dice, waiting for what it brings, except that he has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"19884","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Musab ibn Thabit, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believer on the Day of Resurrection but will come with a Jew or a Christian, saying: This is my ransom from the Fire."
"19885","Abu al-Nadr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, they said: al-Masudi informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named himself names for us, some of which we remembered. He said: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Muqaffi, and al-Hashir, and the Prophet of repentance and battle."
"19886","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Hilal narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, who said: Abu Musa said: O my son, how if you had seen us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and our scent was the scent of sheep."
"19887","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Abu al-Zinad reported that Abu Salamah informed him that Abd al-Rahman ibn Nafi ibn Abd al-Harith al-Khuzai informed him that Abu Musa informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a garden in Medina, upon the edge of the well, dangling his feet. Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, knocked at the door, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So he did, and Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, entered and dangled his feet. Then Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, knocked at the door, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So he did. Then Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, knocked at the door, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and he will meet a trial. So he did."
"19888","Hasan ibn Musa and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umarah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will gather the nations on a plain on the Day of Resurrection, and when it appears to Allah Almighty to separate between His creation, He will represent for every people what they used to worship, and they will follow them until they plunge them into the Fire. Then our Lord Almighty will come to us while we are upon an elevated place, and He will say: Who are you. We shall say: We are the Muslims. He will say: What are you waiting for. They will say: We await our Lord Almighty. He said: He will say: And do you know Him if you see Him. They will say: Yes. He will say: How do you know Him when you have not seen Him. They will say: Yes, He has no equal. He will manifest to us laughing, and He will say: Receive glad tidings, O Muslims, for there is none of you but I have made his place in the Fire a Jew or a Christian."
"19889","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan informed us, from Umarah al-Qurashi, who said: We came as a delegation to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and among us was Abu Burdah, so he fulfilled our need. When Abu Burdah went out, he returned. Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: Remind the elder, what brought you back; did I not fulfill your needs. He said: Abu Burdah said: Except a hadith my father reported to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Allah Almighty will gather the nations on the Day of Resurrection, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Umar said to Abu Burdah: By Allah, did you hear Abu Musa reporting it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, I heard it from my father reporting it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19890","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr informed us, and Husayn ibn Muhammad said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man frees his slave girl then marries her with a new dowry, he has two rewards."
"19891","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, raising it, who said: The orphan girl is consulted concerning herself; if she is silent, she has permitted, and if she refuses, she is not to be married."
"19892","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Rabi, meaning Abu Said al-Nasri, narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, Abu Burdah said: My father reported to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This nation is shown mercy; Allah Almighty made its punishment among itself, and when the Day of Resurrection comes, there will be handed to every man of them a man of the people of the religions, and it will be said: This shall be your ransom from the Fire."
"19893","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abdullah al-Awdi narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, that a man called Hamamah was of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he went out to Isbahan as a raider in the caliphate of Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and he said: O Allah, Hamamah claims he loves meeting You; if Hamamah is truthful, decree for him his truth, and if he is lying, decree upon him, even if unwilling. O Allah, do not return Hamamah from this journey of his. He said: Death seized him, and Affan once said: The belly, and he died in Isbahan. He said: So Abu Musa stood and said: O people, by Allah, we did not hear, in what we heard from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and what our knowledge reached, except that Hamamah is a martyr."
"19894","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu Kabshah, who said: I heard Abu Musa saying upon the pulpit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the good companion is like the perfume seller: if he does not give you, his scent clings to you. And the likeness of the bad companion is like the owner of the bellows."
"19895","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart is only named from its turning. The likeness of the heart is only like a feather hung at the root of a tree, turned by the wind back to belly."
"19896","He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before you are trials like pieces of the dark night; a man will be a believer in them in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. The sitting one in them is better than the standing, and the standing in them is better than the walking, and the walking in them is better than the hastening. They said: So what do you command us. He said: Be the mats of your houses."
"19897","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from al-Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Break your bows and cut your strings, meaning in strife, and stay in the interiors of houses, and be in them as the better of the sons of Adam."
"19898","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of the believer who recites the Quran is like the citron, its taste good and its scent good. And the likeness of the believer who does not recite the Quran is like the date, its taste good and it has no scent. And the likeness of the hypocrite who recites the Quran is like basil, its scent good and it has no taste. And Yahya once said: Its taste bitter. And the likeness of the hypocrite who does not recite the Quran is like the colocynth, it has no scent and its taste foul."
"19899","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, that al-Ashari prayed with his companions a prayer, and a man of the people said when he sat in his prayer: The prayer is joined with righteousness and zakat. When al-Ashari finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: Which of you said such and such words. The people fell silent. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: Aramma is silence. He said: Perhaps you, O Hittan, said it, to Hittan ibn Abdullah. He said: By Allah, I did not say it, and I feared you would rebuke me for it. A man of the people said: I said it, and I meant by it only good. Al-Ashari said: Do you not know what you say in your prayer. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and taught us our practice and explained our prayer to us. He said: Straighten your rows, then let the most reciting of you lead you. When he says the takbir, say the takbir, and when he says: Nor of those astray, say: Amin, Allah will answer you. Then when the imam says the takbir and bows, say the takbir and bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is for that. When he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, Allah will hear for you, for Allah Almighty said upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah hears him who praises Him. And when the imam says the takbir and prostrates, say the takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is for that. When at the sitting, let the first saying of each of you be to say: Greetings, good words, prayers belong to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"19900","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us: Abu Burdah narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Ashari said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two men of the Asharis, one of them on my right and the other on my left, and both of them asked for office, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was using the siwak. He said: What do you say, O Abu Musa, or O Abdullah ibn Qays. He said: I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not inform me of what was in themselves, and I did not know they sought office. He said: It is as if I look at his siwak under his lip, contracted. He said: We do not, or I do not, employ upon our work one who seeks it. But go you, O Abu Musa, or O Abdullah ibn Qays. So he sent him to Yemen, then he followed him with Muadh ibn Jabal. When he came to him, he said: Come down, and he cast for him a cushion, and there was a man with him bound. He said: What is this. He said: He was a Jew, then he became Muslim, then he returned to his religion, the evil religion, and became Jewish. He said: I shall not sit until he is killed, the decree of Allah and His Messenger, three times. So he commanded concerning him and he was killed. Then we discussed standing at night. Muadh ibn Jabal said: As for me, I sleep and stand, or stand and sleep, and I hope in my sleep what I hope in my standing."
"19901","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id from Sufyan, Abu Burda ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burda narrated to me from his grandfather from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: When a beggar or one in need came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Intercede and you will be rewarded, and let Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decree upon the tongue of His Messenger what He wills."
"19902","And he said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"19903","And he said: The trustworthy treasurer who delivers what he is commanded with a willing soul is one of the givers of charity."
"19904","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id and Muhammad ibn Ja'far, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us; Yahya said in his hadith: Amr ibn Murra narrated to me; Ibn Ja'far said: from Murra al-Hamdani, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Many men have attained perfection, and none of the women attained perfection except Maryam bint Imran and Asiya the wife of Fir'awn, and indeed the superiority of A'isha over women is like the superiority of tharid over all other food."
"19905","Haddathana Abu Usama, Abu al-Umays narrated to me from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab from Abu Musa, he said: The day of Ashura was a day the Jews fasted and took as a festival, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast it yourselves."
"19906","Haddathana Abu Usama from Talha ibn Yahya from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, every believer will be given a man from among the people of the religions, and he will say to him: This is your ransom from the Fire."
"19907","Haddathana Abu Dawud al-Hafari, Sufyan narrated to us from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Musa said: I came from Yemen, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I said: With an ihram like the ihram of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He said: Do you have any sacrificial animal with you? He said: I said: meaning no. He said: He commanded me, so I circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa, then I went to a woman from my people and she combed my head and washed it, then I exited ihram. When the day of al-Tarwiya came I entered ihram for Hajj. He said: I used to give fatwa to the people with that during the rule of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both. While I was standing in the market of the season, a man came and spoke to me privately, saying: You do not know what the Commander of the Believers has newly decreed concerning the rites. He said: I said: O people, whoever we gave fatwa to concerning anything, let him wait, for this Commander of the Believers is coming to you, so follow him. He said: He said to me: If we follow the Book of Allah the Exalted, it commands completion, and if we follow the Sunna of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he did not exit ihram until he sacrificed the sacrificial animal."
"19908","Haddathana Waki', Mughira al-Kindi narrated to us from Sa'id from Abu Burda from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, one hundred times every day. Abdullah said: meaning Mughira ibn Abi al-Hurr."
"19909","Haddathana Waki', Shu'ba narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda from his father from Abu Musa, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, I and Mu'adh ibn Jabal, to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, a drink is made in our land called al-mizr from barley, and a drink called al-bit' from honey. He said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"19910","Haddathana Waki', Burayd ibn Abi Burda narrated to me from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes with arrows in the mosque, let him hold their blades."
"19911","Haddathana Abu Usama from Talha ibn Yahya from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, every believer will be given a man from among the people of the religions, and it will be said to him: This is your ransom from the Fire."
"19912","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, Sulayman informed us from al-Hasan from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When two Muslims face each other with their swords and one of them kills the other, both are in the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer, so what of the killed? He said: He intended to kill his companion."
"19913","Haddathana Yazid, Dawud informed us from Abu Nadra from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: Abu Musa sought permission to enter upon Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both, three times, and permission was not given to him, so he returned. Umar met him and said: What is the matter with you, you returned? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks permission three times and permission is not given to him, let him return. He said: You shall bring proof for this or I shall do and do. So he came to the assembly of his people and adjured them by Allah the Exalted, and I said: I am with you, and they testified for him to that, so he let him go."
"19914","Haddathana Yazid, al-Mas'udi informed us, and Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Qasim, al-Mas'udi narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda from his father from his grandfather Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My umma is a mercy-shown umma, upon it in the Hereafter there is no punishment; its punishment is only in this world: killing, tribulations, and earthquakes. Abu al-Nadr said: With earthquakes, killing, and trials."
"19915","Haddathana Yazid, he said: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, Ibrahim ibn Isma'il al-Saksaki narrated to us that he heard Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa, and he accompanied, he and Yazid ibn Abi Kabsha, on a journey, and Yazid used to fast, so Abu Burda said to him: I heard Abu Musa repeatedly say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant falls ill or travels, there is written for him of reward the like of what he used to do resident and healthy."
"19916","Haddathana Affan and Abd al-Samad, they said: Ja'far narrated to us with the meaning; Affan said in his hadith: I heard Abu Imran al-Jawni say: Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, while in the presence of the enemy, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of Paradise are under the shadows of swords. He said: A man from the people, shabby in appearance, stood up and said: O Abu Musa, did you yourself hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this? He said: Yes. He said: He returned to his companions and said: I recite peace upon you, then he broke the scabbard of his sword, then walked with his sword to the enemy and struck with it until he was killed."
"19917","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays from his father from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: In Paradise there is a tent of hollow pearl, its width sixty miles, in every corner of it are inhabitants who do not see the others; the believer will go round to them."
"19918","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu Imran narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two gardens of silver, their vessels and what is in them, and two gardens of gold, their vessels and what is in them, and there is nothing between the people and looking at their Lord the Exalted except the cloak of pride upon His face, Mighty and Majestic, in the Gardens of Eden."
"19919","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us from Abu Imran al-Jawni from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The tent is a pearl, its length into the sky sixty miles, in every corner of it are inhabitants for the believer, and the others do not see them."
"19920","Haddathana Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh, he said: Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Hakim ibn Daylam from Abu Burda from his father, he said: Jews would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sneeze in his presence, hoping he would say to them: May Allah have mercy on you, but he would say to them: May Allah guide you and set right your condition."
"19921","Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah; Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah; he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us from Burayd from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep reciting the Qur'an, for it slips away from the hearts of men more intensely than camels from their halters."
"19922","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, Shu'ba narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda from his father from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Upon every Muslim is charity. They said: If he does not find? He said: He works with his hands, benefits himself, and gives charity. They said: If he does not do or is not able? He said: He helps the one in need, the distressed. He said: If he is not able or does not do? He said: He commands good. They said: If he is not able or does not do? He said: He withholds from evil, for it is charity."
"19923","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, Sufyan narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from his brother from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: Two men from the Ash'aris came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: They began to hint at seeking office, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most treacherous of you with me is he who seeks it."
"19924","Haddathana Abu Qatan, Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Burda said: Abu Musa said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan girl is to be consulted concerning herself; if she remains silent she has given permission, and if she denies she is not to be coerced. I said to Yunus: Did you hear it from him or did you hear it from Abu Burda? He said: Yes."
"19925","Haddathana Bahz, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings and announce glad tidings to the people: whoever says La ilaha illa Allah truthfully from it shall enter Paradise. So they went out announcing glad tidings to the people, and Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, met them, and they gave him glad tidings, but he turned them back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who turned you back? They said: Umar. He said: Why did you turn them back, O Umar? He said: Then the people will rely, O Messenger of Allah."
"19926","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam, Sharik narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He is not from us who shaves, tears, and wails."
"19927","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad, he said: Abu Musa said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, reminded us of a prayer we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), either we forgot it or we abandoned it deliberately; he would say takbir whenever he bowed, whenever he rose, and whenever he prostrated."
"19928","Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah; Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah; Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us from Burayd from Abu Burda from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man praising a man and extolling him in praise, and he said: You have destroyed, or cut, the back of the man."
"19929","Haddathana Abu Abd al-Rahman Mu'ammal, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, Asim narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make Ubayd Abu Amir above most of the people on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Ubayd was killed on the day of Awtas, and Abu Musa killed the killer of Ubayd. He said: Abu Wa'il said: And I hope that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not gather between the killer of Ubayd and Abu Musa in the Fire."
"19930","Haddathana Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Yazid, al-Mas'udi narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: Umar met Asma bint Umays, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both, and said: What fine people you are, were it not that you preceded in emigration and we are better than you. She said: You were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) teaching your ignorant and carrying your foot-soldier, while we fled with our religion. She said: I shall not stop until I enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she entered and mentioned to him what Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, had said to her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather for you is emigration twice: your emigration to Abyssinia and your emigration to Medina."
"19931","Haddathana Hajjaj, Shu'ba narrated to us from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, he said: I heard Abu Burda in the time of al-Hajjaj narrating from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw a funeral being hastened with, and he said: Calmness must be upon you."
"19932","Haddathana al-Qasim ibn Malik Abu Ja'far, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us from Abu Burda, he said: I entered upon Abu Musa in the house of the daughter of Umm al-Fadl, and I sneezed and he did not say tashmit to me, and she sneezed and he said tashmit to her. So I returned to my mother and told her, and when he came to her, she said: My son sneezed in your presence and you did not say tashmit to him, and she sneezed and you said tashmit to her. He said: Your son sneezed and did not praise Allah the Exalted, so I did not say tashmit to him, and she sneezed and praised Allah the Exalted, so I said tashmit to her. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you sneezes and praises Allah, say tashmit to him, and if he does not praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, do not say tashmit to him. She said: You did well, you did well."
"19933","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, he said: Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ja'far, narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves his world harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves his Hereafter harms his world, so prefer what remains over what perishes."
"19934","Haddathana Abu Salama al-Khuza'i, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us from Amr ibn Abi Amr from al-Muttalib from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves his world harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves his Hereafter harms his world, so prefer what remains over what perishes."
"19935","Haddathana Waki', Shu'ba narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh and Abu Musa to Yemen and said: Give glad tidings and do not repel, make easy and do not make difficult, and obey one another and do not differ. He said: Each one of them had a tent in which he would stay, one visiting the other. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I think it is from Abu Musa."
"19936","Haddathana Husayn ibn Ali from Za'ida from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill and his illness grew severe, and he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. A'isha said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; whenever he stands in your place he cannot lead the people in prayer. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are the companions of Yusuf. The messenger came to him, and Abu Bakr led the people in prayer during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19937","Haddathana Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, he said: Za'ida narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Umayr, narrated to us from Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, and he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, and he mentioned it."
"19938","Haddathana Abu Asim, he said: Yunus ibn al-Harith narrated to me, he said: Abu Burda narrated to me from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Prayer upon the back of a mount while traveling is thus and thus and thus and thus."
"19939","Haddathana Abu al-Nadr, Abu Mu'awiya, meaning Shayban, narrated to us from Layth from Abu Burda from Abu Musa from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the noon prayer, then turned to us with his face and said: Stay in your places. He faced the men and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands me to command you to fear Allah and to speak a right word. Then he stepped past the men and came to the women and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands me to command you to fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and to speak a right word. Then he returned to the men and said: When you enter the mosques of the Muslims and their markets, or the markets of the Muslims and their mosques, and you have with you any of these arrows, hold their blades, lest you strike any of the Muslims and harm him or wound him."
"19940","Haddathana Abu Ahmad Husayn ibn Muhammad and Abu al-Nadr, they said: al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-Hasan from Abu Musa, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has changed the color of."
"19941","Haddathana Abu al-Nadr, he said: Abu Mu'awiya, meaning Shayban, narrated to us from Layth from Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a funeral passes by you, whether it is a Muslim or a Jew or a Christian, stand for it, for it is not for it that we stand, but we stand for those with it of the angels."
"19942","Layth said: I mentioned this hadith to Mujahid, and he said: Abd Allah ibn Sakhbara al-Azdi narrated to me, he said: While we were sitting with Ali, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, waiting for a funeral, another passed by us and we stood. Ali, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said: What makes you stand? We said: This is what your companions, the companions of Muhammad, bring us. He said: And what is that? I said: Abu Musa claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a funeral passes by you, whether it is a Muslim or a Jew or a Christian, stand for it, for it is not for it that we stand, but we stand for those with it of the angels. Ali, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that only once, for a man from the Jews, and they were People of the Book and he would imitate them, but when he was forbidden he stopped, and he never did it again after."
"19943","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, he said: Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burda narrated to us from his father from Abu Musa, he said: A beggar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intercede and you will be rewarded, and let Allah decree upon the tongue of His Prophet what He wills."
"19944","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Bishr, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, he said: Ghalib al-Tammar narrated to us from Humayd ibn Hilal from Masruq ibn Aws from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he decreed concerning the fingers ten camels each."
"19945","Haddathana Bakr ibn Isa, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us from Abu Balj, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa al-Ash'ari narrated to us from his father Abd Allah ibn Qays that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the plague and said: A piercing from your enemies among the jinn, and it is the martyrdom of the Muslim."
"19946","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Harb, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Harun Abu Ishaq al-Kufi from Hamdan from Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays in a day and night twelve rak'as apart from the obligatory, a house will be built for him in Paradise."
"19947","Haddathana Asbat ibn Muhammad from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from Abu Burda from his father, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Isra'il informed us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burda from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"19948","Haddathana Marwan ibn Mu'awiya, he said: Thabit ibn Umara narrated to us from Ghunaym ibn Qays from al-Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who perfumes herself and passes by people so they find her scent is an adulteress."
"19949","Haddathana Abda ibn Sulayman, he said: Salih ibn Salih narrated to us from al-Sha'bi from Abu Burda from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a slave girl and disciplines her and disciplines her well, teaches her and teaches her well, then frees her and marries her, has two rewards. And any man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet and believed in Muhammad has two rewards. And any owned slave who fulfills the right of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, upon him and the right of his masters has two rewards."
"19950","Haddathana Waki', he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Qatada from Abu Tamima from Abu Musa."
"19951","Waki' said: And al-Dahhak Abu al-Ala' narrated to me that he heard it from Abu Tamima from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts perpetually, Hell will be constricted upon him thus, and he clenched his fist."
"19952","Haddathana Waki', he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Abu al-Tayyah al-Duba'i, he said: I heard a man he described who used to be with Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Musa wrote to Ibn Abbas: You are a man from the people of your time, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among Banu Isra'il, when one of them was struck by anything from urine he would cut it with shears, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a soft place, meaning soft ground, and urinated in it, and said: When one of you urinates, let him seek a place for his urine."
"19953","Haddathana Waki', he said: Ali ibn Ali ibn Rifa'a narrated to us from al-Hasan from Abu Musa, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be presented on the Day of Resurrection three presentations; as for two presentations, they are argument and excuses, and as for the third, at that the scrolls will fly into the hands, some taking with his right and some taking with his left."
"19954","Haddathana Abu Amir, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us from Asid ibn Abi Asid from Musa ibn Abi Musa al-Ash'ari from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the weeping of the living over him: when the wailing woman says: O my support, O my helper, O my provider, the dead is pulled and it is said to him: Are you her support? Are you her helper? Are you her provider? I said: Glory be to Allah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: No bearer shall bear the burden of another. He said: Woe to you, I narrate to you from Abu Musa from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you say this? Which of us lied? By Allah, I did not lie against Abu Musa, nor did Abu Musa lie against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19955","Haddathana Affan, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Before the Hour is al-harj. They said: And what is al-harj? He said: Killing. They said: More than we kill? We kill in one year more than seventy thousand. He said: It is not your killing of the idolaters, but the killing of some of you by others. They said: And will our minds be with us that day? He said: The minds of most of the people of that time will be taken away, and there will remain dregs of people, most of whom think they are upon something while they are upon nothing. Abu Musa said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I find no way out for me and you from it, if it reaches me and you, except to emerge from it as we entered it, without having shed blood or taken wealth therein."
"19956","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, he said: Asid ibn Abi Asid narrated to me from Ibn Abi Musa from his father, or from Ibn Abi Qatada from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to encircle his beloved with a ring of fire, let him encircle her with a ring of gold, and whoever is pleased to bracelet his beloved with a bracelet of fire, let him bracelet her with a bracelet of gold, but silver, so play with it as you wish."
"19957","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, he said: Imran informed us from Qatada from Abu Burda from Abu Musa that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he feared a man or a people, would say: O Allah, I place You in their throats, and we seek refuge in You from their evils."
"19958","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, he said: Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Qatada from Abu Burda ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays from his father Abd Allah ibn Qays that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he feared a people, would say: O Allah, we place You in their throats, and we seek refuge in You from their evils."
"19959","Haddathana Yunus ibn Muhammad, he said: Abu Layla Abd Allah ibn Maysara narrated to us from Mazida ibn Jabir, he said: My mother said: I was in the mosque of Kufa during the caliphate of Uthman, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, with Abu Musa al-Ash'ari over us. She said: I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting Ashura, so fast."
"19960","Haddathana Hasan, Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam from a man from Banu Tamim from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, led us in prayer, a prayer that reminded us of a prayer we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); either we forgot it or we abandoned it deliberately; he would say takbir in every rising and lowering, standing and sitting."
"19961","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, he said: Jarir narrated to us from Sulayman al-Taymi from Qatada from Abu Ghallab from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us, he said: When you stand for prayer, let one of you lead you, and when the imam recites, be silent."
"19962","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, meaning al-Ashyab, he said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Yazid al-A'raj informed us; Abdullah said: meaning I think him al-Shanni; he said: Hamza ibn Ali ibn Makhfar narrated to us from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: We went on campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) halted us for rest at night. He said: I reached in part of the night the resting place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking him, but did not find him. He said: I went out openly seeking him, and there was a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking what I sought. He said: While we were thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came toward us. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, you are in a land of war and we do not feel safe for you; if only when your need appeared you had told one of your companions, he would have stood with you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I heard a sound like the grinding of a millstone or a humming like the humming of bees, and a comer came to me from my Lord, Mighty and Majestic. He said: He gave me choice between half of my umma entering Paradise and my intercession for them, so I chose my intercession for them, knowing it is broader for them. And He gave me choice between a third of my umma entering Paradise and intercession for them, so I chose for them my intercession, knowing it is broader for them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah the Exalted to make us among the people of your intercession. He said: He supplicated for them both. Then they both awakened the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed them of the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: They began to come to him saying: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah the Exalted to make us among the people of your intercession, and he would supplicate for them. He said: When the people crowded over him and grew many, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is for whoever dies testifying that there is no god but Allah."
"19963","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq, meaning al-Salahini, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us from Abu Sinan, he said: I buried a son of mine, and while I was in the grave Abu Talha took my hand and brought me out, saying: Shall I not give you glad tidings? I said: Yes. He said: al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted said: O Angel of Death, did you take the child of My servant? Did you take the delight of his eye and the fruit of his heart? He said: Yes. He said: What did he say? He said: He praised You and said to Allah we belong and to Him we return. He said: Build for him a house in Paradise and call it the House of Praise."
"19964","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, and he mentioned it, except that he said: Abu Talha al-Khawlani, and he said: al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Arzab."
"19965","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid, he said: Khalid, meaning al-Tahhan, narrated to us from Mutarrif from Amir from Abu Burda from Abu Musa that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning him who frees a slave girl then marries her: He has two rewards."
"19966","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, he said: Huraysh ibn Sulaym informed us, he said: Talha ibn Musarrif narrated to us from Abu Burda from Abu Musa that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"19967","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Safwan ibn Muhriz, he said: Abu Musa said: I am free from whom Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are free, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is free from whoever shaves, wails, and tears."
"19968","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhada narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour are trials like pieces of dark night; a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening therein, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. The sitting in them is better than the standing, the standing better than the walking, the walking better than the running. So break your bows, cut your strings, and strike your swords against stones, and if one of you is entered upon in his house, let him be like the better of the two sons of Adam."
"19969","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Abu Qudama al-Harith ibn Ubayd al-Iyadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran, meaning al-Jawni, narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gardens of al-Firdaws are four: two of gold, their ornament, vessels, and what is in them, and two of silver, their vessels, ornament, and what is in them. There is nothing between the people and looking at their Lord, Mighty and Majestic, except the cloak of pride upon His face in the Garden of Eden. And these rivers gush from the Garden of Eden, then split thereafter into rivers."
"19970","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Abu Daris Sahib al-Jawr narrated to us, he said: Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa narrated to us from Abu Musa that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray two rak'as after Asr."
"19971","Haddathana Abu Nu'aym, he said: Badr ibn Uthman, a freedman of the family of Uthman, narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa narrated to me from his father from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A questioner came to him asking about the times of prayer, and he did not answer him anything. He commanded Bilal, who called the iqama for Fajr when dawn split while people could hardly know one another. Then he commanded him and he called iqama for Zuhr when the sun declined, while one saying would say midday has come or not yet, and he was more knowledgeable than them. Then he commanded him and he called iqama for Asr while the sun was high. Then he commanded him and he called iqama for Maghrib when the sun set. Then he commanded him and he called iqama for Isha when the twilight disappeared. Then he delayed Fajr the next day until he finished it while one saying would say the sun has risen or almost. He delayed Zuhr until it was near the time of Asr of the previous day. Then he delayed Asr until he finished it while one saying would say the sun has reddened. Then he delayed Maghrib until it was at the disappearance of twilight, and delayed Isha until it was the first third of the night. Then he called the questioner and said: The time is between these two."
"19972","Haddathana Zayd ibn al-Hubab, he said: Ibn Thawban narrated to us from his father from Makhul, he said: Abu A'isha, who was a companion of Abu Hurayra, narrated to me that Sa'id ibn al-As invited Abu Musa al-Ash'ari and Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both, and said: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say takbir in al-Fitr and al-Adha? Abu Musa said: He would say four takbirs, his takbir over funerals, and Hudhayfa confirmed him. Abu A'isha said: I never forgot after his saying: his takbir over funerals, while Abu A'isha was present with Sa'id ibn al-As."
"19973","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given five: I was sent to the red and the black, the earth was made for me a purification and a mosque, spoils were made lawful for me and were not made lawful for those before me, I was aided with terror for a month, and I was given intercession. There is no prophet but has asked for intercession, and I have hidden my intercession, then made it for whoever of my umma dies not associating anything with Allah."
"19974","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, meaning al-Zubayri, he said: Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned its meaning, but did not chain it."
"19975","Haddathana Yunus ibn Muhammad, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was using the siwak, placing the tip of the siwak upon his tongue, brushing toward above. Hammad described as though raising his siwak. Hammad said: Ghaylan described it to us, he said: He would brush lengthwise."
"19976","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burda from Abu Musa, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, forgive me my sins, my ignorance, my excess in my affair, and what You know better than I. O Allah, forgive me my seriousness and jest, my error and intent, all of that is with me."
"19977","Haddathana Ziyad ibn Abd Allah, meaning al-Bakka'i, he said: Mansur narrated to us from Shaqiq ibn Salama from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was bowed head, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what is fighting in the way of Allah the Exalted? For one of us fights out of zeal and fights out of anger, is there reward for him? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to him, and were it not that he was standing, or he was sitting, the doubt is from Zuhayr, he would not have raised his head to him, and said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"19978","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to us from Abu Wa'il, he said: Abu Musa said: A man asked, or a man came to, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting bowed head, and said: What is fighting in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic? For one of us fights out of zeal and anger, is there reward for him? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to him, and were it not that he was standing, or he was sitting, the doubt is from Zuhayr, he would not have raised his head to him, and said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"19979","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Harb, he said: Umar ibn Ali ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: Abu Umays narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda from his father from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he said: People from the Ash'aris came to me and said: Go with us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for we have a need. He said: I stood with them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, employ us in your service. I excused myself to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for what they said, saying: I did not know what their need was. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) believed me and excused me, saying: We do not employ in our service one who asks for it."
"19980","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Musa and Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Yemen, saying to them: Make easy and do not make difficult, give glad tidings and do not repel, and obey one another. Abu Musa said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land in which a drink is made from honey called al-bit', and a drink from barley called al-mizr. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"19981","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, he said: A man from my people narrated to me; Shu'ba said: I used to remember his name; he said: We were at the door of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, waiting for permission to enter upon him, and I heard Abu Musa al-Ash'ari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The passing of my umma is by piercing and plague. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, this piercing we know, so what is plague? He said: The piercing of your enemies among the jinn, and in each is martyrdom. Ziyad said: I was not satisfied with his saying, so I asked the chief of the quarter, who was with them, and he said: He spoke truthfully; Abu Musa narrated it to us."
"19982","Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ilaqa narrated to us from Usama ibn Sharik, he said: We went out, a dozen or so from Banu Tha'laba, and there we were with Abu Musa, and he was narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, make the passing of my umma in plague, and he mentioned it."
"19983","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiya, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Abu Musa, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey. He said: We descended a hollow of the land. He said: The people raised their voices with takbir, and he said: O people, be gentle with yourselves, for you do not call upon one deaf nor absent; you call upon One hearing, near. He said: Then he called me, and I was near him, saying: O Abd Allah ibn Qays, shall I not guide you to a word from the treasures of Paradise? He said: I said: Yes. He said: There is no might nor power except with Allah."
"19984","Haddathana Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad, he said: Yunus narrated to us from Abu Burda from Abu Musa that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"19985","Haddathana Abd al-Wahid and Rawh ibn Ubada, they said: Thabit ibn Umara narrated to us from Ghunaym ibn Qays from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; Rawh said: He said: I heard Ghunaym, he said: I heard Abu Musa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who perfumes herself then passes by people so they find her scent is an adulteress."
"19986","Haddathana Abd al-Wahid and Rawh, they said: Thabit ibn Umara narrated to us from Ghunaym ibn Qays from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; Rawh said: I heard Ghunaym, he said: I heard Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every eye is adulterous."
"19987","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, informed us from Abu al-Salil from Zahdam from Abu Musa, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking mounts, and he said: No, by Allah, I shall not mount you. When we returned, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to us three camels with white humps. He said: I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore not to mount us, then he mounted us. So we came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore not to mount us, yet you mounted us. He said: I did not mount you, but Allah mounted you. By Allah, I do not swear an oath and see another better than it except I do it. Abu al-Salil is Durayb ibn Nuqayr."
"19988","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Dawud informed us from Abu Nadra from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: Abu Musa sought permission to enter upon Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, three times, and permission was not given to him, so he returned. Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, met him and said: What is the matter with you, you returned? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks permission three times and permission is not given to him, let him return. He said: You shall bring proof for this or I shall do and do. So he came to the assembly of his people and adjured them by Allah the Exalted, and I said: I am with you, and they testified for him, so he let him go."
"19989","Haddathana Yazid, he said: Sa'id informed us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When two Muslims face each other with their swords and one of them kills the other, both are in the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer, what of the killed? He said: He intended to kill his companion."
"19990","Haddathana Yazid, he said: al-Mas'udi informed us from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda from his father from his grandfather Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My umma is a mercy-shown umma, upon it in the Hereafter there is no punishment, except its punishment in this world is killing, tribulation, and earthquakes."
"19991","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: al-Awwam informed us, and Muhammad ibn Yazid with the meaning, he said: al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il al-Saksaki narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa, while he was saying to Yazid ibn Abi Kabsha, and they accompanied one another on a journey, and Yazid would fast while traveling, Abu Burda said to him: I heard Abu Musa repeatedly say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the Muslim servant falls ill or travels, there is written for him of reward as he used to do resident and healthy. Muhammad, meaning Ibn Yazid, said: Allah wrote the like of what he used to do resident and healthy."
"19992","Haddathana Yazid, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us from Thabit al-Bunani from Abu Burda from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes by a market or assembly or mosque with arrows, let him grasp their heads, let him grasp their heads, three times. Abu Musa said: Tribulation did not cease with us until some of us aimed them at the faces of others."
"19993","Haddathana Yazid, he said: al-Jurayri informed us from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and we hastened the return and gained good spoils. When we overlooked al-Ruzdaq, each man among us began to say takbir, I think he said: with the loudest voice, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, and he began to say with his hand thus, and Yazid described as though gesturing, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, you do not call upon one deaf nor absent; He Whom you call is beneath the necks of your mounts. Then he said: O Abd Allah ibn Qays, or O Abu Musa, shall I not guide you to a word from the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: There is no might nor power except with Allah."
"19994","Haddathana Yazid, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us from Thabit al-Bunani, he said: One who heard Hittan ibn Abd Allah narrating from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrated to me, he said: I said to a man: Come, let us make this day of ours for Allah, Mighty and Majestic. By Allah, it is as though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) witnessed this day and addressed, saying: And among them is one who says: Come, let us make this day of ours for Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He kept saying it until I wished the earth would swallow me."
"19995","Haddathana Yazid, he said: al-Jurayri informed us from Ghunaym ibn Qays from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This heart is like a feather in a desert land, the wind turns it back to belly. My father said: Isma'il did not raise it from al-Jurayri."
"19996","Haddathana Rawh, he said: Sa'id narrated to us from Qatada, he said: Abu Burda ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays narrated from his father, he said: My father said: Had you witnessed us while we were with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when rain struck us, you would have thought our smell the smell of sheep, for our clothing was only wool."
"19997","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us from Qatada from Abu Burda, he said: Abu Musa said to me: O my son, had you seen us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and rain struck us, you would have found from us the smell of sheep."
"19998","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Thabit narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us from Abu Mijlaz, he said: Abu Musa led his companions in prayer while departing from Mecca to Medina, praying Isha two rak'as and saluting, then standing and reciting one hundred verses from Surat al-Nisa in one rak'a. That was disapproved to him, and he said: I did not fail to place my feet where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his foot, and to do the like of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did."
"19999","Haddathana Abd al-Samad and Affan, they said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us that Abu Bakr, and Affan said: from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays al-Ash'ari, informed him from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tent is a hollow pearl, its length into the sky sixty miles, in every corner are inhabitants for the believer whom the others do not see."
"20000","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to us, and he mentioned the like. The end of the hadith of Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and it is the end of the Musnad of the Kufis."
